$TTL 3D
; Rogue authoritative zone for example.net served by the attacker's
; name server (ns.attacker32.com / 10.9.0.153).
; After the cache-poisoning attack injects "example.net NS ns.attacker32.com",
; the victim resolver sends ALL future example.net lookups here, so every
; name under the hijacked domain resolves to an attacker-controlled host.
@       IN      SOA   ns.attacker32.com. admin.attacker32.com. (
                2025101101  ; Serial
                8H          ; Refresh
                2H          ; Retry
                4W          ; Expire
                1D)         ; Minimum TTL

@       IN      NS    ns.attacker32.com.

@       IN      A     192.168.0.100        ; example.net
www     IN      A     192.168.0.100        ; www.example.net -> attacker host
mail    IN      A     192.168.0.100        ; mail.example.net -> attacker host
*       IN      A     192.168.0.100        ; everything else -> attacker host
